# Create Components With Base Rule

Use when building components that extend or compose with MasterFabric base classes.

## Base Classes to Use

| Base Class | Use For |
|------------|---------|
| `MasterViewCubit<V, S>` | Full-screen views with scaffold |
| `BaseViewModelCubit<S>` | Cubits / view models |
| `MasterScaffoldWidget` | Custom scaffold layouts |
| `LoadingView`, `ErrorHandlingView`, `EmptyView` | Pre-built state UIs |
| `BlocProvider`, `BlocBuilder`, `BlocListener` | BLoC integration |

## Composing With Pre-built Views

```dart
// Loading state
if (state.status == MyStatus.loading) return const LoadingView();

// Error state
if (state.status == MyStatus.error) {
  return ErrorHandlingView(error: state.errorMessage);
}

// Empty state
if (state.items?.isEmpty ?? true) {
  return EmptyView(message: 'No items found');
}
```

## Using MasterScaffoldWidget

```dart
MasterScaffoldWidget(
  scaffoldMessengerKey: key,
  appBar: AppBar(title: Text('Title')),
  body: content,
  useSafeArea: true,
  horizontalPadding: const PaddingVisibility.enabled(),
  navbarSpacer: const SpacerVisibility.enabled(),
  footerSpacer: const SpacerVisibility.enabled(),
)
```

## Widgets That Use Cubit/State

```dart
class MyComponent extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return BlocBuilder<MyCubit, MyState>(
      buildWhen: (prev, curr) => prev.status != curr.status,
      builder: (context, state) {
        return _buildFromState(state);
      },
    );
  }
}
```

## Layout Visibility Types

- `SpacerVisibility.enabled()` / `.disabled()` - Navbar/footer spacers
- `PaddingVisibility.enabled(value: 24.0)` / `.disabled()` - Horizontal/vertical padding
- `AppBarPaddingVisibility` - App bar padding when SafeArea disabled

## Spacer Types

- `CoreSpacerType.navbar` - Top safe area
- `CoreSpacerType.footer` - Bottom safe area
- `CoreSpacerType.content` - Content spacer

## Checklist

- [ ] Extend correct base (MasterViewCubit for views, BaseViewModelCubit for cubits)
- [ ] Use pre-built LoadingView, ErrorHandlingView, EmptyView where appropriate
- [ ] Use MasterScaffoldWidget for custom layouts
- [ ] BlocBuilder/buildWhen to avoid unnecessary rebuilds
- [ ] Follow import order: Dart → Flutter → packages → masterfabric_core → relative
